    "created_at": "2018-09-12T05:54:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-12T05:54:53Z",
    "body": "Interop for margins is horrible at the moment, so we're free to spec whatever. :)\r\nIgnoring them seemed like one compelling option, making it easy to deal with.\r\n\r\nBut I agree that margins could be useful. But then let's specify that they don't collapse with anything on the outside (It's already implicit that they don't collapse with anything on the inside the legend, since legends establish a BFC).\r\n\r\nWe also need to spec how this affects alignment with the fieldset border. Are we still going to use the legend *border* box for alignment? I guess so? And the margins contribute to the size of the size of the block-start border area of the fieldset (just like the remaining parts (border box) of the legend), right?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/420521294/reactions",
